  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice.\r\rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the approved plans including plans(s) that may have been revised, as set out in the attached schedule which forms part of this notice.\r\rENC012-BLL-01-XX-DR-A-2001 Rev A\rENC012-BLL-01-XX-DR-A-2003\rENC012-BLL-01-GF-DR-A-1001 Rev A\rENC012-BLL-01-XX-DR-A-2004\rENC012-BLL-01-XX-DR-A-2002\rENC012-0001\r0002\rEnvironmental Noise Survey and Plant Noise Assessment Report\rAcoustic Fence Modules\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "All new external works shall be carried out in materials that resemble, as closely as possible in colour and texture to those used in the existing building, unless otherwise specified in the approved plans.\r\rReason: To safeguard the appearance of the premises and the character of the immediate area.\r",
    "Prior to the use of the air conditioning units hereby approved,  details of the proposed acoustic enclosure, including an acoustic report and details of design, must be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The acoustic report must demonstrate by calculation or measurement that the acoustic enclosure ensures that the noise from the combined air conditioning units is at least 5dB below the typical background sound pressure level stated in the acoustic report submitted with the planning application at the nearest residential window, which includes windows at Bridgewood House.\r\rReason: To protect residents from noise and disturbance and in the interests of visual amenity. \r",
    "Prior to the installation of the AC units and enclosure hereby approved, a Tree Protection Plan and landscape retention plan, demonstrating how exisiting trees and landscaping in the immedaite vicinity (particularly the semi-mature tree on the street corner) is to be protected during the period of construction, shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Authority. The development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details. \r\rReason: In order to maintain the health of the existing trees and landscaping which provide important screening for the development\r"
  ],
